---
// The homepage's "why this name" moment. The film itself is no longer *here* —
// it is the background of the whole site (src/components/SiteFilm.astro) — so
// this section is deliberately transparent: `data-film-wash="0.34"` is the
// thinnest wash anywhere on the page, which lets the film come forward behind the
// copy for one screen before the content sections quieten it down again.
---
<section class="section story-section" id="story" data-film-wash="0.34" aria-labelledby="story-title">
  <div class="container center">
    <span class="eyebrow gold"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-spark"/></svg> Wisdom Through Education</span>
    <h2 class="section-title" id="story-title">Named After <span class="grad-text">Saraswati</span></h2>
    <p class="section-sub">
      Sarasvi takes its name from Saraswati, the goddess of knowledge, music and the arts. The 20-second
      film behind this page was made in her name — scroll, and it plays behind you, frame by frame. Scroll
      back up and it rewinds.
    </p>
    <p class="story-actions">
      <button class="btn btn-dark" type="button" data-film-sound>
        <svg class="icon"><use href="#i-volume"/></svg> Watch with sound
      </button>
      <span class="story-note"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-play"/></svg> Muted as you scroll · it keeps time with the page</span>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
